model law03
  tally 2
  on 2026-10-25
  start 2022-01-01
  end 2022-12-31
  note "Probe LAW-03: a mid-year law change with a transitional rule that runs the old version beside the new and keeps the lower advance."
  note "The card's law and facts are stipulations, known from start (L 4.5). The old and the new version govern spans that don't overlap."

source card "Probe card LAW-03 (tmp/cases/probes/law/LAW-03.md): story, rules 1-4 and question"

unit DUK: currency minor 0.01

index emp = [ania, ola]

index mo = month 2022-01..2022-12

input old_last_day: date question "On what day does the old version last govern?"

input pay_base[e in emp]: money DUK question "What is the employee's monthly base?"

input rate: num question "What advance rate is in force?"

input relief: money DUK question "What monthly relief is in force?"

def adv[e in emp, m in mo]: money DUK at start_of(m)
  note "the advance the payroll keeps: the formula under the month's own law, or, under rule 3, the lower of that and the formula under the old version's law, on the same base"
  rule base = formula[e]
  rule transitional beats base v card_transitional = min(formula[e], formula[e] as if {law old_last_day})

def formula[e in emp]: money DUK at reader
  note "rules 1-2 and 4: the rate times the base less the relief, rounded half up to 0.01, with the rate and the relief in force on its reader's law date (L 4.3: at reader, so a law pin reaches it)"
  rule base v card_rules = round(rate * pay_base[e] - relief, minor(DUK), half-up)

ask advances: adv[ania, 2022-06], adv[ania, 2022-07], adv[ola, 2022-07] law 2022-07-01

ask july_sides: formula[e] as if {law 2022-06-30}, formula[e] for e in emp law 2022-07-01

ask june_unchanged: check adv[ania, 2022-06] == adv[ania, 2022-06] as if {wording 2022-06-30 for [adv, rate, relief]} law 2022-07-01

version card_facts
  cite card
  governs always
  known 2022-01-01
  pay_base[ania] = 8000 "story: Ania's base is 8 000.00"
  pay_base[ola] = 2000 "story: Ola's 2 000.00"

version card_new
  cite card
  governs 2022-07-01..
  known 2022-01-01
  note "rule 2: the new version, from 1 July 2022; it enters into force on 1 July, the later of known and the start of governs (L 5.3)"
  rate = 0.12 "rule 2: 12 % of the base"
  relief = 0 "rule 2: no relief"

version card_old
  cite card
  governs ..2022-06-30
  known 2022-01-01
  note "rule 1: the old version, to 30 June 2022"
  old_last_day = 2022-06-30 governs always "rule 1: old version, to 30 June 2022"
  rate = 0.17 "rule 1: 17 % of the base"
  relief = 300 "rule 1: minus a monthly relief of 300.00"

version card_rules
  cite card
  governs always
  known 2022-01-01
  note "rules 1-2 and 4: no items; the advance formula's rule points at it (the figures are each version's rows; rule 4 rounds half up to 0.01)"

version card_transitional
  cite card
  governs 2022-07..2022-12
  known 2022-01-01
  note "rule 3: no items; the transitional rule of adv points at it. July to December 2022 the payroll computes both and keeps the lower"
